.TH "tum\-defs" "5" "" "" "tmux\-borrow Manual"
.SS NAME
tum\-defs [em] the tum utility (\f[CR].util\f[R]) and layout
(\f[CR].layout\f[R]) definition file format
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[CR]\[ti]/.config/tum/<name>.util\f[R]
.PP
\f[CR]\[ti]/.config/tum/<name>.layout\f[R]
.SS DESCRIPTION
Definitions live in one directory [em] \f[CR]\[ti]/.config/tum/\f[R]
(\f[CR]XDG_CONFIG_HOME\f[R] is respected) [em] with one file per utility
(\f[CR]<name>.util\f[R]) and one file per layout
(\f[CR]<name>.layout\f[R]).
Utilities and layouts share the directory.
.PP
The format is flat \f[CR]key:value\f[R], one entry per line: no
sections, no hierarchy, no quoting.
The \f[B]filename is the name\f[R]; there is no \f[CR]name:\f[R] field
inside the file, so name collisions are impossible.
Layouts reference utility files by name; there is no repetition.
.PP
Comments: everything after \f[CR]#\f[R] on a line is ignored.
A \f[CR]#\f[R] must be precedced by whitespace or start the line, so
values containing \f[CR]#\f[R] (such as a URL fragment) are not split.
.SS UTILITY FILE KEYS
The special keys below are reserved.
Every \f[B]other\f[R] \f[CR]key:value\f[R] line is an \f[B]environment
key\f[R] [em] it sets an environment variable for the launched process
(see ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES).
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
lw(23.3n) lw(23.3n) lw(23.3n).
